            "question": "How long does delivery take?",
            "answer": "In-stock pieces ship within 2 working days and reach most Indian cities in 3–6 days, and delivery is free on orders above ₹7,500. Made-to-order and custom pieces take 3–5 weeks.",
            "answer_richtext": "",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I return a handloom piece?",
            "answer": "Yes. Unworn pieces with tags can be returned within 14 days. Customised, altered and pet pieces are final sale unless they arrive damaged.",
            "answer_richtext": "",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why are there small irregularities?",
            "answer": "Hand processes leave traces: a slightly soft ikkat edge, a tiny slub in the cloth. These are signs of real handwork, not defects.",
            "answer_richtext": "",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I care for handloom?",
            "answer": "Cotton and mul: gentle wash, dry in shade. Silk, Banaras, Muga and chiffon: dry clean first, store folded in muslin and refold every few months.",
            "answer_richtext": "",
            "open_by_default": false
          }
